                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ed337749-f4a1-3086-8d37-a8078be8647c",
                        "entry_id": "852d7873-6b76-3bbc-87b5-8f1134914385",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To reach an advanced stage of decomposition."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "85a991e4-3771-4706-9d57-c11320a91921",
                                "sense_id": "ed337749-f4a1-3086-8d37-a8078be8647c",
                                "text": "In the Middle Ages, for instance, a recipe for sex stimulation required the putrefied flesh of a human corpse, together with both human and animal testes and ovaries, pimento, and alcohol."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ccc398f1-6fe2-3ed6-beb6-692c5f6dfacf",
                        "entry_id": "852d7873-6b76-3bbc-87b5-8f1134914385",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To become gangrenous."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7ca9d8b7-52d7-35af-8b86-eb1d362bedfc",
                        "entry_id": "852d7873-6b76-3bbc-87b5-8f1134914385",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To make morbid, carious, or gangrenous."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d4966786-0665-40c0-92ed-d3ae413c23f5",
                                "sense_id": "7ca9d8b7-52d7-35af-8b86-eb1d362bedfc",
                                "text": "to putrefy an ulcer or wound"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d1dd276f-2651-31cb-be54-04a524a82a4e",
                        "entry_id": "852d7873-6b76-3bbc-87b5-8f1134914385",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To corrupt; to make foul."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "06941680-ff6d-476b-be30-d10693ad51d0",
                                "sense_id": "d1dd276f-2651-31cb-be54-04a524a82a4e",
                                "text": "Private suits do putrefy the public good."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d753d4a4-3cd2-4207-b248-4f596b34ecf9",
                                "sense_id": "d1dd276f-2651-31cb-be54-04a524a82a4e",
                                "text": "They would but stink, and putrefy the air."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
